Apache License, Version 2.0.

Modifications made by Raiku:

  * Removed the ShredStream deprecation kill switch (the hard-coded
    September 5, 2026 shutdown date, the `shutdown_has_passed()` check and the
    associated startup abort) introduced upstream in commit b96e369.
  * Trimmed the program to forward-only operation. Removed the `shredstream`
    subcommand, the Jito Block Engine heartbeat client, the Ed25519 token
    authenticator, the shred reconstruction (deshred) pipeline and the gRPC
    entry-streaming server, along with their command-line flags and metrics.
  * Renamed the crate and binary from `jito-shredstream-proxy` to
    `raiku-shredstream-proxy`, and the `jito-protos` crate to
    `raiku-shred-protos`.
  * Replaced the `jito_protos/protos` git submodule (jito-labs/mev-protos) with
    a vendored, reduced `shredstream.proto` containing only the `TraceShred`
    message.
  * Removed the `solana-ledger` dependency on the jito-foundation/jito-solana
    branch `eric/v2.2-merkle-recovery`; all Solana crates now resolve from
    crates.io.
